## 4. Conclusion
The chitosan- $\mathbf{\nabla}\cdot\mathbf{g}.$ -PNVCL/ ZIF-8 nanofibers synthesized by electrospinning method have been applied for the removal of As(V), $\mathrm{Cr(VI)}$ and phenol from aqueous solutions. The obtained results revealed that the adsorption process using synthesized composite nanofibrous adsorbent could be applied as an effective method for the removal of metal ions and phenol under optimum ZIF-8 concentration of $3\mathrm{wt.}\%$ , $\mathrm{pH}$ of 3, contact time of 30 min for metal ions sorption and 40
min for phenol removal.  The surface adsorption, pore filling mechanism, ion exchange and $\pi{-}\pi$ stacking were responsible for the removal of metal ions and phenol from water. The obtained results indicated that the synthesized nanofibrous adsorbent was able for simultaneous removal of adsorbates. The adsorption efficiency chitosan- $\mathbf{g}$ -PNVCL/ ZIF-8 nanofibers for the removal of adsorbates in the both single and ternary systems was in order of $\mathrm{Cr(VI){>}A s(V){>}}.$ phenol.
